# Keep every dot file and dot directory (.github, .claude, .clang-tidy,
# .gitignore at any depth, ...) out of the source tarball GitHub generates from
# a tag via git archive. Distributions repackage that tarball and reject the
# clutter (GH #2068, #2101, #2272). It is one pattern rather than a list of
# names because a list was what kept going wrong: each release added a new dot
# file that nobody remembered to list here. A pattern without a slash matches
# the name at any depth, and export-ignore on a directory drops all of it.
# The source_tarball_has_no_dotfiles ctest checks the result.
.* export-ignore
